WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Phase three results for an investigational, amelin, peptide medicine in diabetes and obesity were released this week. Welcome to the very first episode of Peptides Weekly. Today is September 23rd, 2026. A peptide is a short chain of amino acids. The term now covers approved medicines such as insulin, as well as vial sold online under research use only labels. This show explains what each compound is, how researchers study it, and what the data shows.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.360
at each level of evidence. Insulin serves as one clear example because it's regulatory

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:41.220
status, manufacturing record, and clinical observations are documented across peer-reviewed

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:47.200
sources. The show stays strictly with education and never supplies doses, schedules, combinations,

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:54.140
sources, or protocols. It never tells anyone to start, stop, or change a treatment. Every

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:58.340
named compound carries the regulatory status stated in the source material.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:04.300
Peptides weekly belongs to the Narra Network, an independent and ad-free set of programs.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:09.320
Novel Nordisk reported new Phase III data on an Amelon-based candidate.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.760
A randomized Phase III trial tested an investigational Amelon peptide candidate

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.840
in adults with obesity or diabetes.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.940
The company stated the results moved the program closer to potential human use.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.160
The findings remain at the Phase III randomized human trial level.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.680
The source for these statements appears in reports linked from x.com.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:37.520
Two randomized human trials examined oral semaglutide, a GLP-1 peptide, in patients with

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.880
modeled Alzheimer's disease.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.440
The trials carried the name evoke.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.540
Neither trials showed slowing of disease progression.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.880
The result is a negative finding from phase 3 randomized trials.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.040
The source for these statements appears in the Lancet.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:58.540
An animal study measured neuro-tensin signaling and gut function in a rodent model of type 2 diabetes.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.460
The measurements focused on altered gastrointestinal function.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.060
The measurements also focused on neuro-tensin signaling.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.080
The work used an experimental rodent model.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.920
The work is at the experimental animal level.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:17.300
The source for these statements appears in the peptides journal via sciencedirect.com.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:24.100
A rodent study tested an oral ureotensin-2 receptor antagonist in a dietary model of liver disease.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.060
The compound carried the designation KR36996.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:35.980
KR36996 is described as an orally active ureotensin-2 receptor antagonist.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.540
The study examined attenuation of hepatic inflammation and fibrosis.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:46.440
The dietary model used a methionine and coline-deficient diet to induce fibrosync's

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:51.820
diato hepatitis. The evidence is at the animal study level. Researchers gave

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:56.640
phoenixin 14 to rodents with chemically induced pancreatitis and recorded

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.360
changes in inflammation and cell death markers. The study recorded changes in

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.480
inflammation markers. The study recorded changes in oxidative stress

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:12.520
markers. The model used L-arginine to induce acute pancreatitis. The data come from an animal model.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:18.440
This week's spotlight centers on insulin, a peptide hormone whose signaling pathway appears

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:25.640
in many metabolic disease studies. One longitudinal observational study followed 17 Pima Indians whose

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:32.440
glucose tolerance deteriorated from normal to impaired to diabetic over an average of 5.1 years.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:37.840
Transition from normal to impaired glucose tolerance coincided with increased body weight

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.840
and reduced insulin sensitivity.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:45.940
Insulin secretion remained relatively preserved until later stages in that human observational

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:46.560
study.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:51.180
Indogin is glucose output rose as tolerance worsened in the same study.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.720
mitochondrial function was tracked in a separate time course study using Otsuka Long Evans

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:00.400
Tokushima fatty rats and their non-hyperfagic controls.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:06.220
cycles. At five weeks of age, hepatic mitochondrial respiration and enzyme activities were already

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:11.980
reduced in the obese strain. Insulin resistance and stiotosis developed only at later ages

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:17.180
in that rodent time course study. Insulin-like growth factor one was measured in a field

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:23.880
study of 669 wild so-A sheep lambs, sampled at approximately four months of age across

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:30.620
nine summers. Higher circulating IGF-1 concentrations correlated with faster early growth rates

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:37.180
and higher over-winter survival in that observational field study of animals. The association held

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:43.560
after accounting for cohort and environmental variation. Additional observational work examined

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:49.360
insulin resistance patterns in women with prior miscarriage and in elderly adults stratified

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:54.900
by obesity status. Post-prandial insulin resistance showed stronger links to miscarriage

00:04:54.900 --> 00:05:01.360
history than fasting measures alone in one multi-center cohort. Sex differences in basal insulin

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:07.400
secretion emerged more clearly in obese versus non-obese elderly groups. None of these studies

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:13.940
establish causal mechanisms or test therapeutic interventions. Insulin is an approved biologic medicine.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:20.440
The supplied sources do not establish regulatory status or long-term outcome data for any newer

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:24.560
peptide that match the breadth of human observations accumulated for insulin.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:30.720
No source reports oral formulations reaching approval or documents specific manufacturing

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:31.580
transitions.

